Hi! Starting from Qt 5.2.0 (most probably from rc1 and definitely not f=
rom=20
beta1 currently in experimental) Qt5 will switch qreal from float to do=
uble on=20
arm*.

We have the option to keep some archs in float by passing a compilation=
=20
parameter. I've done so for armel and sh4, so only armhf will switch to=
=20
double.

Of course we are still on time to discuss this, and this is the reason =
of this=20
mail. What do you think WRT the above changes?

On the other hand, if the above change is kept, symbols for Qt5 on armh=
f=20
managed with pkg-kde-tools' symbolshelper will need an explicit double =
for=20
armhf instead of using qreal's subst. This is because on Qt4 qreal will=
 be=20
kept as float.

Any feedback will be kindly appreciated.

Kinds regards, Lisandro.

--=20
